#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096413 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096613 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a71301e9-bc7f-53b9-900e-c3bd37f96b03" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6624681a-bb00-59db-8df9-4d5a3cd00434" :question/math-academy-id "e-3627" :question/problem "Given that $y=5\\ln x$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{ \\textrm{d} x}\\left( \\ln x \\right)= \\dfrac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}   & = \\left(5\\ln x\\right)'\\  \n                                                    & = 5 (\\ln x)'\\\n                                                    &=5\\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}\\\n                                                    &= \\dfrac{5}{x}.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t  \n\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096414 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/id #uuid "58d47fb0-cf75-58c4-8eea-f3ae97333159" :question/math-academy-id "e-3628" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2\\ln x+x^2-1$, find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\tf'(x) &= \\left(2\\ln x+x^2-1\\right)'\\\n\t\t\t&=2 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{x}+2x-0\\\n\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{2}{x}+2x.\n\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096415 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/id #uuid "f61ac550-d62c-558f-b6d5-0d4c9aba8089" :question/math-academy-id "e-3629" :question/problem "Given that $y=4\\log_3 x,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply our formula for the derivative when the base of the logarithm is a number other than $e.$ By doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}&=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x \\ln 3}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{4}{x \\ln 3}.\n\n}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096416 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096616 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "5eaa00f8-0fd0-5de6-a7c0-965db6de3a5c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3630" :question/problem "Given that $y= \\log_4 x + \\ln x$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( \\log_4 x + \\ln x \\right)\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\log_4 x) + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\ln x )\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 4} + \\dfrac{1}{x}.\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}+\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{ln⁡4}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1045aaaf-0a76-5469-afdc-876ec049ae29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11}^{x}-ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284929} {:answer/id #uuid "aa30aba2-91df-575b-9e42-a1c8a2d47cbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11}^{x}ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286338} {:answer/id #uuid "c13aff45-c853-5d8b-ae11-7b4d6befdcb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "ln⁡11+\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286556} {:answer/id #uuid "eff2509a-f3c8-5644-a073-b8761ffb95e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11}^{x}ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286990} {:answer/id #uuid "ff507140-fe41-5deb-989d-ac21680f83b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eff2509a-f3c8-5644-a073-b8761ffb95e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{11}^{x}ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286990} :answer-field/id #uuid "38feddcb-991e-5fb6-9fb0-47bd31940554" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1cb4423b-343c-5035-85a6-f38acaa8835d" :question/math-academy-id "q-1919" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={11}^{x}-5ln⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({11}^{x}-5ln⁡x) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}\\cdot ln⁡11-5(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={11}^{x}ln⁡11-\\frac{5}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8847ec53-1ef1-5244-9261-3db213a50ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5e^{x}\\ln x + \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094916} {:answer/id #uuid "af4a5664-c507-5fd9-af8c-e68ce9129a6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5e^{x}\\ln - 5 + \\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094917} {:answer/id #uuid "d160ad97-ce05-5c09-a415-37e669bc37d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{x} + \\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094918} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f5dc19-0891-5c65-ba47-3963e6e0a451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5e^{x} - \\ln 3 + \\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094919} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb7af8c-26aa-56d2-9b2c-2028d177a3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5e^{x} + \\frac{2}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094920}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e0978740-9d55-5364-bce6-ab2f65f0ed46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094915}] :question/id #uuid "e09c4141-d749-574e-b1a3-1f49f5b7e3d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-1920" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for $y =-5e^{x} + 2\\ln x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096615 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277904a9-9e9e-53f0-a87c-616303962482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "277904a9-9e9e-53f0-a87c-616303962482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312275} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb11537-ff22-5776-85db-c4e4d92da407" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9fb0b98-97be-5fa4-a0a8-73b036fd9d03" :question/math-academy-id "q-339994" :question/problem "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡6} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =6(3)^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡6} \\\\  & =55-\\frac{1}{ln⁡6}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096614 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83ce3c28-857b-5538-b362-cf52526e3688" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Sum Containing a Natural Logarithm Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39500646-122f-5de4-a3f8-1b1dfa91aa61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39500646-122f-5de4-a3f8-1b1dfa91aa61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312439} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1560d5a-5716-563a-970a-84ea931d3b0b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "905686ba-b3f6-58e7-998d-63ec7c2c2866" :question/math-academy-id "q-340104" :question/problem "Given the function  $y=4ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}+5$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4ln⁡x-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}+5) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{4}{x}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{x}ln⁡(2))|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {2}^{2}ln⁡(2) \\\\  & =2-\\frac{4}{3}ln⁡(2)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
